#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. Introduction {#1-introduction}"
msgstr "1. Introduction {#1-introduction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bits, gates, and circuits are the basic building blocks of quantum "
"computing. You will learn quantum computation with the circuit model using "
"quantum bits and gates, and also review the superposition, measurement, and "
"entanglement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Les bits, les portes et les circuits sont les blocs de construction "
"fondamentaux du calcul quantique. Tu apprendras le calcul quantique avec le "
"modèle de circuits en utilisant des bits quantiques et des portes, et tu "
"reverras également la superposition, la mesure et l'intrication.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson you will learn:\n"
"- Single-qubit gates\n"
"- Bloch sphere\n"
"- Superposition\n"
"- Measurement\n"
"- Two-qubit gates and entanglement state\n"
msgstr ""
"Dans cette leçon, tu apprendras :\n"
"- Les portes à qubit unique\n"
"- La sphère de Bloch\n"
"- La superposition\n"
"- La mesure\n"
"- Les portes à deux qubits et l'état d'intrication\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At the end of this lecture, you will learn about circuit depth, which is "
"essential for utility-scale quantum computing.\n"
msgstr ""
"À la fin de ce cours, tu apprendras la profondeur de circuit, qui est "
"essentielle pour le calcul quantique à l'échelle utilitaire.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Computation as a diagram {#2-computation-as-a-diagram}"
msgstr "2. Le calcul comme un diagramme {#2-computation-as-a-diagram}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When using qubits or bits, we need to manipulate them in order to turn the "
"inputs we have into the outputs we need. For the simplest programs with very"
" few bits, it is useful to represent this process in a diagram known as a "
"*circuit diagram*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lorsqu'on utilise des qubits ou des bits, il faut les manipuler pour "
"transformer les entrées dont on dispose en les sorties dont on a besoin. "
"Pour les programmes les plus simples comportant très peu de bits, il est "
"utile de représenter ce processus sous la forme d'un diagramme connu sous le"
" nom de *diagramme de circuit*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bottom-left figure is an example of a classical circuit, and the bottom-"
"right figure is an example of a quantum circuit. In both cases, the inputs "
"are on the left and the outputs are on the right, while the operations are "
"represented by symbols. The symbols used for the operations are called "
"“gates”, mostly for historical reasons.\n"
msgstr ""
"La figure en bas à gauche est un exemple de circuit classique, et la figure "
"en bas à droite est un exemple de circuit quantique. Dans les deux cas, les "
"entrées sont à gauche et les sorties à droite, tandis que les opérations "
"sont représentées par des symboles. Les symboles utilisés pour les "
"opérations sont appelés « portes », principalement pour des raisons "
"historiques.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![\"classical logic and quantum circuit\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-"
"scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/classical-vs-quantum.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![\"circuit logique classique et circuit "
"quantique\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-"
"gates-and-circuits/classical-vs-quantum.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Single-qubit quantum gate {#3-single-qubit-quantum-gate}"
msgstr "3. Porte quantique à qubit unique {#3-single-qubit-quantum-gate}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"3.1 Quantum state and Bloch sphere {#31-quantum-state-and-bloch-sphere}"
msgstr ""
"3.1 État quantique et sphère de Bloch {#31-quantum-state-and-bloch-sphere}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A qubit's state is represented as a superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and "
"$|1\\rangle$. An arbitrary quantum state is represented as\n"
msgstr ""
"L'état d'un qubit est représenté comme une superposition de $|0\\rangle$ et "
"$|1\\rangle$. Un état quantique arbitraire est représenté par\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\alpha|0\\rangle+ \\beta|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\alpha|0\\rangle+ \\beta|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are complex numbers such that "
"$|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"où $\\alpha$ et $\\beta$ sont des nombres complexes tels que "
"$|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ are vectors in the two-dimensional complex "
"vector space:\n"
msgstr ""
"$|0\\rangle$ et $|1\\rangle$ sont des vecteurs dans l'espace vectoriel "
"complexe à deux dimensions :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"|1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"|1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Therefore, an arbitrary quantum state is also represented as\n"
msgstr ""
"Par conséquent, un état quantique arbitraire est également représenté par\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} + \\beta\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} + \\beta\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From this, we can see that the state of a quantum bit is a unit vector in a "
"two-dimensional complex inner product space with an orthonormal basis of "
"$|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$. It is normalized to 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"De là, on peut voir que l'état d'un bit quantique est un vecteur unitaire "
"dans un espace produit intérieur complexe à deux dimensions, avec une base "
"orthonormale formée de $|0\\rangle$ et $|1\\rangle$. Il est normalisé à 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\psi\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha^* & \\beta^*\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\\n"
"\\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = 1\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\psi\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha^* & \\beta^*\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\\n"
"\\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = 1\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ |\\psi\\rangle =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}$ is also called the statevector.\n"
msgstr ""
"$ |\\psi\\rangle =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}$ est également appelé le vecteur d'état (statevector).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A single-qubit quantum state is also represented as\n"
msgstr "Un état quantique à qubit unique est aussi représenté par\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"=\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}|0\\rangle+e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}|1\\rangle\n"
"=\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\ e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"=\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}|0\\rangle+e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}|1\\rangle\n"
"=\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\ e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\theta$ and $\\varphi$ are the angles of the Bloch sphere in the "
"following figure.\n"
msgstr ""
"où $\\theta$ et $\\varphi$ sont les angles de la sphère de Bloch dans la "
"figure suivante.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/bloch.avif)\n"
"In the next few code cells, we will build up basic calculations from constituent pieces in Qiskit. We'll construct an empty circuit and then add quantum operations, discussing the gates and visualizing their effects as we go.\n"
"You can run the cell by \"Shift\" + \"Enter\". Import the libraries first.\n"
msgstr ""
"![Sphère de Bloch](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/bloch.avif)\n"
"Dans les prochaines cellules de code, nous allons construire des calculs de base à partir d'éléments constitutifs dans Qiskit. Nous construirons un circuit vide, puis ajouterons des opérations quantiques, en discutant des portes et en visualisant leurs effets au fur et à mesure.\n"
"Tu peux exécuter la cellule avec \"Shift\" + \"Entrée\". Commence par importer les bibliothèques.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the quantum circuit {#prepare-the-quantum-circuit}"
msgstr "Préparer le circuit quantique {#prepare-the-quantum-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We will create and draw a single-qubit circuit.\n"
msgstr "Nous allons créer et dessiner un circuit à qubit unique.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/fdef9137-9e39-4b05-afa9-9091766053f6-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Sortie de la cellule de code précédente](/learning/images/courses/utility-"
"scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/fdef9137-9e39-4b05-afa9-9091766053f6-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "X gate {#x-gate}"
msgstr "Porte X {#x-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The X gate is a $\\pi$ rotation around the $x$ axis of the Bloch sphere.\n"
"Applying the X gate to $|0\\rangle$ results in $|1\\rangle$, and applying the X gate to $|1\\rangle$ results in $|0\\rangle$, so it is an operation similar to the classical NOT gate, and is also known as bit flip. The matrix representation of the X gate is below.\n"
msgstr ""
"La porte X est une rotation de $\\pi$ autour de l'axe $x$ de la sphère de Bloch.\n"
"Appliquer la porte X à $|0\\rangle$ donne $|1\\rangle$, et appliquer la porte X à $|1\\rangle$ donne $|0\\rangle$ ; c'est donc une opération similaire à la porte NOT classique, également connue sous le nom de bit flip. La représentation matricielle de la porte X est la suivante.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/b3468430-0cbc-44ab-bd21-901436662a4b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Sortie de la cellule de code précédente](/learning/images/courses/utility-"
"scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/b3468430-0cbc-44ab-bd21-901436662a4b-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In IBM Quantum&reg;, the initial state is set to $|0\\rangle$, so the "
"quantum circuit above in matrix representation is\n"
msgstr ""
"Dans IBM Quantum&reg;, l'état initial est $|0\\rangle$, donc le circuit "
"quantique ci-dessus en représentation matricielle est\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X|0\\rangle=  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\ 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = |1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X|0\\rangle=  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\ 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = |1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next, let's run this circuit using a statevector simulator.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ensuite, exécutons ce circuit en utilisant un simulateur de vecteur "
"d'état.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/efb727e8-f51e-4903-aa0f-e4c099316815-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Sortie de la cellule de code précédente](/learning/images/courses/utility-"
"scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/efb727e8-f51e-4903-aa0f-e4c099316815-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Vertical vector is displayed as row vector, with complex numbers (the "
"imaginary part is indexed by $j$ ).\n"
msgstr ""
"Le vecteur vertical est affiché comme vecteur ligne, avec des nombres "
"complexes (la partie imaginaire est indexée par $j$ ).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "H gate {#h-gate}"
msgstr "Porte H {#h-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Hadamard gate is a $\\pi$ rotation around an axis halfway between the "
"$x$ and $z$ axes on the Bloch sphere. Applying the H gate to $|0\\rangle$ "
"creates a superposition state such as $\\frac{|0\\rangle + "
"|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}$. The matrix representation of the H gate is below.\n"
msgstr ""
"La porte Hadamard est une rotation de $\\pi$ autour d'un axe à mi-chemin "
"entre les axes $x$ et $z$ sur la sphère de Bloch. L'application de la porte "
"H à $|0\\rangle$ crée un état de superposition tel que $\\frac{|0\\rangle + "
"|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}$. La représentation matricielle de la porte H est la "
"suivante.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/574c35f0-26a9-423a-8d65-7140ba7398e3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Sortie de la cellule de code précédente](/learning/images/courses/utility-"
"scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/574c35f0-26a9-423a-8d65-7140ba7398e3-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
"quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/7adf0e93-6db3-4aa8-800f-c91c8cc46001-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Sortie de la cellule de code précédente](/learning/images/courses/utility-"
"scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-"
"outputs/7adf0e93-6db3-4aa8-800f-c91c8cc46001-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is\n"
"$$\n"
"H|0\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\n"
"0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"C'est\n"
"$$\n"
"H|0\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\n"
"0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This superposition state is so common and important, that it is given its "
"own symbol:\n"
msgstr ""
"Cet état de superposition est si courant et important qu'il possède son "
"propre symbole :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|+\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|+\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By applying the $H$ gate on the $|0\\rangle$, we created a superposition of "
"$|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ where measurement in the computational basis "
"(along z in the Bloch sphere picture) would give you each state with equal "
"probabilities.\n"
msgstr ""
"En appliquant la porte $H$ à $|0\\rangle$, nous avons créé une superposition"
" de $|0\\rangle$ et $|1\\rangle$ où une mesure dans la base computationnelle"
" (le long de z dans la représentation de la sphère de Bloch) donnerait "
"chaque état avec des probabilités égales.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$|-\\rangle$ state {#rangle-state}"
msgstr "État $|-\\rangle$ {#rangle-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You might have guessed that there is a corresponding  $|-\\rangle$ state:\n"
"$$\n"
"|-\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{|0\\rangle -|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
"To create this state, first apply an X gate to make $|1\\rangle$, then apply an H gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tu as peut-être deviné qu'il existe un état $|-\\rangle$ correspondant :\n"
"$$\n"
"|-\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{|0\\rangle -|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Pour créer cet état, applique d'abord une porte X pour obtenir $|1\\rangle$, puis applique une porte H.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-"
